WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.870
Look at a distant hill.

2
00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.560
Now look at a book held close.

3
00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:10.660
Your eye refocuses in an instant, yet the
distance from lens to retina never changes.

4
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.330
Instead, muscles change
the shape of the eye lens.

5
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:19.190
So why does short sight, or myopia,
need a lens that spreads light out,

6
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.140
rather than focusing it?

7
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:24.130
In this mission, you'll
trace light through the eye,

8
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.240
from the cornea to the retina.

9
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:30.820
Then you'll map the range of vision,
from the near point to the far point.

10
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:35.870
Your mission: explain why a lens that
spreads light out corrects myopia.
